    {
      "id": "LZE-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-local-dirichlet-expansion",
      "title": "The local Dirichlet expansion and the principal pole",
      "statement": "At 101/100+it the radius 2/5 gives a multiplicity count in radius 2/15 and an expansion on radius 1/15. The negative logarithmic derivative has the principal-character pole with positive sign and each zero pole with negative multiplicity. The remainder is O(log(m(|t|+2))).",
      "hypotheses": "Every m≥3, every character modulo m and every real t with one absolute constant. The principal function is regularized at 1. The logarithmic-derivative formula is evaluated at s≠1 with the regularized L-function nonzero.",
      "dependencies": [
        "LZE-01"
      ],
